    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44758" root="&#xA;                        ومى&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوَامٍ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>Lands wherein is nothing.</i> (A'Obeyd,
TA, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بلق</span>.) The pl., when indeterminate,
is thus, not <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوَامِى</span>. See a verse in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عرى</span>,
conj. 12. [This is a correction of art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">موم</span>, to
which this word, and also the verb, belong: for
there is no such root as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ومى</span>.]

